module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeTwistRigidity.Basic

/-!
# Rigidity of the degree-one twist, with no multiplicativity hypothesis

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidity.eq_id` forces a family of endomorphisms
`α n : 𝒪(n) ⟶ 𝒪(n)` of the graded twists on `Proj 𝒜` to consist of identity morphisms from two
hypotheses: the family fixes the global sections attached to the homogeneous elements, and it is
**multiplicative**. The second hypothesis is an equation about the canonical product of two
arbitrary local sections of two twists, and it is the expensive one — for a composite of
comparison maps it asks that each structural factor commute with the comparison between an
inverse image of a tensor product and the tensor product of the inverse images, which nothing in
this development supplies.

In the single degree `n = 1` the hypothesis can be dropped **entirely**, with nothing put in its
place beyond what the geometry already gives. The reason is that `α 1` is a morphism of sheaves of
`𝒪`-modules, so it is `𝒪(V)`-linear on the sections over every open for free; and near any point
at which some degree-one element `g` does not vanish, `𝒪(1)` is *freely generated by one section*
— the global section `degreeSection 𝒜 1 g` that `g` itself determines
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv.bijective_smul_degreeOneSection`, Tag 01MS). So every
local section of `𝒪(1)` there is `r • degreeSection 𝒜 1 g`, and `α 1` fixes it as soon as it fixes
that one generator. No product of two sections of two twists ever appears.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.app_eq_self_of_le_basicOpen`: on an open
  contained in the standard open of a degree-one element whose own global section is fixed, `α 1`
  is the identity on sections.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.app_eq_self` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id`: **rigidity in degree one with no
  multiplicativity hypothesis.** The one hypothesis is that at every point of `Proj 𝒜` there is a
  degree-one element, nonvanishing there, whose global section the family fixes.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.exists_degreeOne_notMem_of_adjoin_eq_top` and
  `eq_id_of_adjoin_eq_top`: generation in degree one supplies the geometric half of that
  hypothesis, so it is not vacuous — and for a graded ring generated in degree one the only
  condition left is that the family fix the global section of each degree-one element.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id_of_generates`: the same with the fixing
  hypothesis taken relative to a graded ring homomorphism `ψ`, which must generate `𝒜` pointwise.
  Only degree one of `ψ` is used, and the degree-one elements are supplied by the ambient graded
  ring rather than by `ψ`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id_res`: **the geometric instance** — for a
  nested pair of affine opens of the base of a quasi-coherent graded algebra, the drop-in
  replacement for `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeTwistRigidity.eq_id_res` in degree one.

## Why only degree one, and what the hypothesis replaces

The generation-and-cancellation proof of the general statement writes a local section of `𝒪(n)` as
a fraction `β / c` with `β` and `c` homogeneous, and cancels `c` by multiplying with the section
that `c` determines; that multiplication is a product of two twist sections, so it needs
multiplicativity. Here the cancellation is done by a *division* instead: with `g` of degree one
nonvanishing nearby, `β / c = (β / (c g)) · (g / 1)` and the first factor has degree `0`, so it is
a section of the structure sheaf and the equation is an instance of `𝒪`-linearity. Tag 01MS's
trivialization packages exactly that division, so no fraction is manipulated below.

The same argument runs in every degree `n ≥ 0` for which `𝒜` has a nonvanishing element of degree
`n` near each point, which for a graded ring generated in degree one is every such `n`; it is
stated here in degree one because that is the degree the twist `𝒪_{𝐏(E)}(1)` of Tag 01VM and the
first condition of Tag 01W8 ask for, and because in degree one the trivialization's free generator
is the canonical section of a degree-one element rather than of a power of one.

For negative `n` the argument fails and the statement is false without further input: `𝒪(n)` has no
nonvanishing global section of the right degree to divide by.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv.degreeOneSection` carries the twist index in the form
`(1 : ℤ) * ((1 : ℕ) : ℤ)` that Tag 01MS's trivialization writes, and the statements below carry it
as `(1 : ℤ)`. The two are definitionally equal, and the transparency attributes repeated from the
twist files are what lets the elaborator see it; no transport across the two spellings is written.

The single fixing hypothesis is consumed through
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeTwistRigidity.app_eq_self_of_values_mkOne'`, which takes exactly
one fixed global section rather than all of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidity.FixesDegreeSections`. That matters: the relative
statements below cannot assume the absolute fixing hypothesis, because upgrading the relative one
to it is precisely the step that consumes multiplicativity.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01MS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01MS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NO)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NR)

## What is not done here

This file removes the multiplicativity hypothesis from rigidity in degree one; it does not supply
either hypothesis of rigidity for any particular family.
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartTransRelativeProj.IsNestedCocycle` at `n = 1` is still open, and
what it is still missing has changed, so the state is recorded exactly.

* The computation of Tag 01NO's **named** comparison morphism on a pulled-back homogeneous global
  section is now done, as
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjInclusionDegreeSection.projInclusionTwistMap_degreeSection`. The
  same identity for `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ChartTransRelativeProj.pushNested`, over an open of
  the relative Proj, is still owed, and it is the structural half of the cocycle rather than its
  mathematical content.
* What is also still missing — and this is independent of the cocycle — is the `hdeg` hypothesis of
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id_res` for the graded algebra in question.
  For the symmetric algebra of a quasi-coherent module it is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjRepresentsF1.IsGeneratedInDegreeOne` of
  `Stacks.SymGraded.schemeSheafGradedAlgebra`, via
  `exists_degreeOne_notMem_of_adjoin_eq_top` below — and that predicate occurs in this repository
  only ever as a hypothesis and is nowhere proved for `Sym`. So the remark above that generation in
  degree one "holds for the symmetric algebra of a module" is a statement about the mathematics,
  not about the library.

No `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.TwistData` is constructed and no project tag is
attached to any declaration below.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistSections
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne

universe u u' w w' v

variable {R : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing R] [SetLike σ R] [AddSubgroupClass σ R]
  {𝒜 : ℕ → σ} [GradedRing 𝒜]

attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose
attribute [local implicit_reducible]
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureSheaf
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top

variable {α : ∀ n : ℤ, twistingSheaf 𝒜 n ⟶ twistingSheaf 𝒜 n}

/-- **The local step.** Let `g` be homogeneous of degree one and suppose the family fixes the
global section of `𝒪(1)` that `g` determines. Then on every open contained in the standard open
`D₊(g)` the family is the identity on the sections of `𝒪(1)`.

Tag 01MS trivializes `𝒪(1)` over `D₊(g)` by multiplication by that very section
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv.bijective_smul_degreeOneSection`), so a section there
is `r • degreeSection 𝒜 1 g` for a unique section `r` of the structure sheaf; `α 1` is
`𝒪`-linear, being a morphism of sheaves of modules, so it fixes the multiple as soon as it fixes
the generator. No multiplicativity enters. -/
public theorem app_eq_self_of_le_basicOpen {g : R} (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 1)
    (hfix : (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op ⊤) (degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩) = degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩)
    {W : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜)} (hW : W ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g)
    (t : (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.obj (op W)) :
    (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op W) t = t := by
  have hgen : (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op W) (ProjDegreeOneTriv.degreeOneSection 𝒜 hg hW) =
      ProjDegreeOneTriv.degreeOneSection 𝒜 hg hW :=
    RelativeTwistRigidity.app_eq_self_of_values_mkOne' (α := α) (m := (1 : ℤ)) (N := 1) rfl hg
      hfix W (ProjDegreeOneTriv.degreeOneSection 𝒜 hg hW)
      (fun y => degreeSection_apply 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩ ⟨y.1, trivial⟩)
  obtain ⟨r, hr⟩ := (ProjDegreeOneTriv.bijective_smul_degreeOneSection 𝒜 hg hW).surjective t
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg ((α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op W)) hr.symm) (Eq.trans ?_ hr)
  exact Eq.trans (((α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op W)).hom.map_smul r _)
    (congrArg (fun z : (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.obj (op W) => r • z) hgen)

/-- **Rigidity in degree one on sections, with no multiplicativity hypothesis.** If at every point
of `Proj 𝒜` there is a homogeneous element of degree one which does not vanish there and whose
global section the family fixes, then the family is the identity on the sections of `𝒪(1)` over
every open.

The element may be chosen anew at each point, which is what makes the hypothesis reachable: a
single degree-one element working everywhere would be a nonvanishing global section of `𝒪(1)`,
which `Proj 𝒜` need not have. -/
public theorem app_eq_self
    (hpt : ∀ x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜, ∃ (g : R) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 1),
      g ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal ∧
      (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op ⊤) (degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩) = degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩)
    (V : Opens (ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜)) (t : (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.obj (op V)) :
    (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op V) t = t := by
  refine Subtype.ext (funext fun x => ?_)
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hnv, hfixg⟩ := hpt x.1
  have hmem : x.1 ∈ V ⊓ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g := ⟨x.2, hnv⟩
  have hle : V ⊓ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ V := inf_le_left
  have hlocal := app_eq_self_of_le_basicOpen hg hfixg (inf_le_right :
      V ⊓ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g ≤ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g)
    ((twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hle).op t)
  calc ((α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op V) t).1 x
      = ((twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hle).op
          ((α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op V) t)).1 ⟨x.1, hmem⟩ := rfl
    _ = ((α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op (V ⊓ ProjectiveSpectrum.basicOpen 𝒜 g))
          ((twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hle).op t)).1 ⟨x.1, hmem⟩ :=
          TwistRigidity.twist_val_congr 𝒜
            (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (α (1 : ℤ)).val (homOfLE hle).op t).symm _
    _ = ((twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)).val.map (homOfLE hle).op t).1 ⟨x.1, hmem⟩ :=
          TwistRigidity.twist_val_congr 𝒜 hlocal _
    _ = t.1 x := rfl

/-- **Rigidity in degree one, with no multiplicativity hypothesis.** A family of endomorphisms of
the graded twists on `Proj 𝒜` is the identity in degree one as soon as, at every point, some
degree-one element nonvanishing there has its global section fixed. -/
public theorem eq_id
    (hpt : ∀ x : ProjectiveSpectrum.top 𝒜, ∃ (g : R) (hg : g ∈ 𝒜 1),
      g ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal ∧
      (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op ⊤) (degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩) = degreeSection 𝒜 1 ⟨g, hg⟩) :
    α (1 : ℤ) = 𝟙 (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)) :=
  SheafOfModules.hom_ext (PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun V =>
    ModuleCat.hom_ext (LinearMap.ext fun t => app_eq_self hpt V.unop t))

/-- **Generation in degree one supplies the geometric half of the hypothesis.** If `𝒜` is
generated in degree one over its degree-zero part then at every point of `Proj 𝒜` some
homogeneous element of degree one does not vanish.

This is what makes the hypothesis of `eq_id` and of the relative statements below non-vacuous: it
holds for the symmetric algebra of a module, which is the graded algebra whose relative `Proj` is
the projective bundle. It is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv`'s
`exists_mem_basicOpen_degreeOne` read as a non-membership in the point's homogeneous ideal. -/
public theorem exists_degreeOne_notMem_of_adjoin_eq_top
    (hadj : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set R) = ⊤) (x : ProjectiveSpectrum 𝒜) :
    ∃ a : 𝒜 1, (a : R) ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal :=
  ProjDegreeOneTriv.exists_mem_basicOpen_degreeOne 𝒜 hadj x

/-- **Rigidity in degree one for a graded ring generated in degree one.** The hypothesis of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id` is then reduced to the fixing condition
alone: the family need only fix the global section of every degree-one element. -/
public theorem eq_id_of_adjoin_eq_top (hadj : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (𝒜 1 : Set R) = ⊤)
    (hfix : ∀ a : 𝒜 1, (α (1 : ℤ)).val.app (op ⊤) (degreeSection 𝒜 1 a) = degreeSection 𝒜 1 a) :
    α (1 : ℤ) = 𝟙 (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)) := by
  refine eq_id fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := exists_degreeOne_notMem_of_adjoin_eq_top hadj x
  exact ⟨(a : R), a.2, ha, hfix a⟩

/-! ### Relative to a graded ring homomorphism -/

section Res

variable {R' : Type u'} {σ' : Type w'} [CommRing R'] [SetLike σ' R'] [AddSubgroupClass σ' R']
  {ℬ : ℕ → σ'} [GradedRing ℬ]

omit [AddSubgroupClass σ' R'] [GradedRing ℬ] in
/-- **Rigidity in degree one, relative to a graded ring homomorphism, with no multiplicativity
hypothesis.** The family need only fix the global sections attached to the images of
`ψ : ℬ →+*ᵍ 𝒜`; what is assumed of `𝒜` itself is that at every point of `Proj 𝒜` some element of
degree one does not vanish.

Generation turns the second into the hypothesis of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne.eq_id`: a degree-one `a` nonvanishing at `x`
becomes, after multiplication by a degree-zero image of `ψ` nonvanishing at `x`, an image of `ψ`
of degree one; the product is nonvanishing at `x` because the homogeneous ideal of `x` is prime,
and its global section is fixed because it is an image of `ψ`. Only degree one and degree zero of
`ψ` are used. -/
public theorem eq_id_of_generates {ψ : ℬ →+*ᵍ 𝒜}
    (hdeg : ∀ x : ProjectiveSpectrum 𝒜, ∃ a : 𝒜 1, (a : R) ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal)
    (hgen : RelativeTwistRigidity.Generates ψ)
    (hfix : RelativeTwistRigidity.FixesResDegreeSections ψ α) :
    α (1 : ℤ) = 𝟙 (twistingSheaf 𝒜 (1 : ℤ)) := by
  refine eq_id fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hdeg x
  obtain ⟨d, c, hnvd, heq⟩ := hgen 1 a x
  have hmemg : (a : R) * ψ (d : R') ∈ 𝒜 1 := by
    rw [heq]
    exact ψ.map_mem c.2
  exact ⟨(a : R) * ψ (d : R'), hmemg,
    Submonoid.mul_mem (Ideal.primeCompl x.asHomogeneousIdeal.toIdeal) ha hnvd,
    RelativeTwistRigidity.fixes_of_eq_res hfix 1 c ⟨(a : R) * ψ (d : R'), hmemg⟩ heq⟩

end Res

/-! ### The geometric instance: a nested pair of affine opens of the base -/

section Nested

variable {X : Scheme.{v}} (A : SheafGradedAlgebra X) (U V : X.Opens) (h : U ≤ V)
  (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V)

include hU hV

/-- **Relative rigidity in degree one for a nested pair of affine opens, with no multiplicativity
hypothesis.** The drop-in replacement, in degree one, for
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeTwistRigidity.eq_id_res` and for
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDS.eq_id_res`: a family of endomorphisms of the twists on
`Proj Γ(U, A)` which fixes the global sections attached to the restrictions of the homogeneous
elements over a larger affine open is the identity in degree one, provided the graded ring of
sections over `U` has, at every point of its `Proj`, a nonvanishing element of degree one.

That proviso holds for the symmetric algebra of a quasi-coherent module — the graded algebra whose
relative Proj is the projective bundle — since a symmetric algebra is generated in degree one; see
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjDegreeOneTriv.exists_mem_basicOpen_degreeOne`, which derives it from
generation in degree one for any graded ring. -/
public theorem eq_id_res
    {α : ∀ n : ℤ, twistingSheaf (A.grading U) n ⟶ twistingSheaf (A.grading U) n}
    (hdeg : ∀ x : ProjectiveSpectrum (A.grading U),
      ∃ a : (A.grading U) 1, (a : A.sectionRing U) ∉ x.asHomogeneousIdeal)
    (hfix : RelativeTwistRigidity.FixesResDegreeSections (A.res h) α) :
    α (1 : ℤ) = 𝟙 (twistingSheaf (A.grading U) (1 : ℤ)) :=
  eq_id_of_generates hdeg (RelativeTwistRigidity.generates_res A U V h hU hV) hfix

end Nested

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistRigidityDegreeOne

end
